Wicked and tyrannical.

782
00:53:30,400 --> 00:53:32,200
May Allah protect all of us.

783
00:53:32,200 --> 00:53:37,200
The second person, wa ghalin fideen.

784
00:53:40,020 --> 00:53:43,140
Ghalin fideen barikun minhum.

785
00:53:43,540 --> 00:53:45,140
Ghalin fideen.

786
00:53:45,880 --> 00:53:49,920
The one who goes into extremes in the matters of the religion.

787
00:53:52,100 --> 00:53:54,900
Is an extremist in the matters of the religion.

788
00:53:56,060 --> 00:53:58,900
How? I give you one small example.

789
00:53:59,620 --> 00:54:03,340
One of the places where the prophet sallallahu alayhi wa ala salam

790
00:54:03,340 --> 00:54:07,080
mentioned clear extremism in the deen

791
00:54:07,080 --> 00:54:11,320
was a person who was selecting stones

792
00:54:11,320 --> 00:54:14,180
that were bigger than the tip of the small finger

793
00:54:14,420 --> 00:54:17,180
on the day of stoning the Jamarads.

794
00:54:17,640 --> 00:54:19,040
He was picking big stones.

795
00:54:19,480 --> 00:54:20,560
People said, it's ghalou.

796
00:54:20,980 --> 00:54:22,140
Yes, you are to stone.

797
00:54:22,580 --> 00:54:25,560
But these stones have gone beyond the stones

798
00:54:25,560 --> 00:54:27,720
that you have been commanded to stone.

799
00:54:29,520 --> 00:54:32,200
So when a person goes beyond limits.

800
00:54:33,000 --> 00:54:34,480
Let me give us another example.

801
00:54:34,680 --> 00:54:38,340
Yes, we are encouraged to observe qiyamun laid.

802
00:54:39,260 --> 00:54:43,600
The prophet sallallahu alayhi wa ala salam told us about qiyamun laid.

803
00:54:44,240 --> 00:54:48,720
In a lot of ahadith, how about the one who does not sleep?

804
00:54:49,380 --> 00:54:50,920
He prays throughout the night.

805
00:54:51,140 --> 00:54:53,100
This is ghalou fideen.

806
00:54:53,100 --> 00:54:57,580
It's ghalou fideen, not to sleep at all, it's ghalou.

807
00:54:58,980 --> 00:55:02,720
The same way we are encouraged to fast during the daytime, are we?

808
00:55:04,100 --> 00:55:07,040
How about the one who every day is fasting?

809
00:55:08,220 --> 00:55:09,540
Every day is fasting.

810
00:55:10,640 --> 00:55:11,520
So look at him.

811
00:55:11,980 --> 00:55:14,080
Every day he is fasting during daytime.

812
00:55:15,300 --> 00:55:17,860
Every day he is on qiyamun laid.

813
00:55:17,900 --> 00:55:18,660
He is not sleeping.

814
00:55:18,920 --> 00:55:21,280
The prophet condemned it, sallallahu alayhi wa ala salam.

815
00:55:22,000 --> 00:55:24,180
Another aspect of ghalou fideen.

816
00:55:24,720 --> 00:55:27,220
A man has a wife and he never comes near her.

817
00:55:28,220 --> 00:55:31,660
Or a woman who never allows her husband to come near her.

818
00:55:31,660 --> 00:55:32,040
Why?

819
00:55:32,240 --> 00:55:33,840
She is busy with ibadah.

820
00:55:34,360 --> 00:55:36,460
I'm busy with ibadah.

821
00:55:36,460 --> 00:55:38,700
I'm busy with ibadah.

822
00:55:39,100 --> 00:55:43,300
And all of these, these are aspects of ghalou fideen.

823
00:55:43,640 --> 00:55:47,500
You see that ghalou, the basics of that thing will be there.

824
00:55:47,500 --> 00:55:50,940
But you'll be doing it in a manner that goes beyond limits.

825
00:55:51,760 --> 00:55:52,460
Like fasting.

826
00:55:52,800 --> 00:55:53,840
Yes, we should fast.

827
00:55:54,340 --> 00:55:55,260
Beyond limit.

828
00:55:55,760 --> 00:56:00,180
No fasting should go beyond fast a day, live a day.

829
00:56:00,600 --> 00:56:02,020
That's so mudawud.

830
00:56:03,160 --> 00:56:05,140
Except you fast three days in a month.

831
00:56:06,100 --> 00:56:09,440
Maybe one at the beginning, one at the middle, one at the end.

832
00:56:10,240 --> 00:56:12,300
Or you fast three straight days.

833
00:56:13,320 --> 00:56:15,960
Whether at the beginning or at the middle or at the end.

834
00:56:16,980 --> 00:56:18,720
These fasts are allowed.

835
00:56:19,360 --> 00:56:22,500
For that a man is fasting every day of the month.

836
00:56:23,360 --> 00:56:26,080
The only time you can do that is in Ramadan.

837
00:56:26,900 --> 00:56:29,560
Except maybe the first ten days of Zulhija again.

838
00:56:30,140 --> 00:56:31,100
Those ones are straight.

839
00:56:31,580 --> 00:56:36,560
And even in that you are going to exempt two days from those first ten days of Zulhija.

840
00:56:37,720 --> 00:56:39,780
The day of Nahar, the tenth day.

841
00:56:40,360 --> 00:56:45,100
Because we have been prohibited from fasting on the tenth day of Zulhija.

842
00:56:45,100 --> 00:56:47,680
You are also going to exempt a Saturday.

843
00:56:48,620 --> 00:56:52,500
Because we have also been prohibited not to fast on Saturday.

844
00:56:52,620 --> 00:56:54,820
Except a fast that is compulsory.

845
00:56:55,880 --> 00:56:57,980
So all these are aspects of gulu.

846
00:56:58,760 --> 00:57:00,360
A person goes beyond limits.

847
00:57:00,740 --> 00:57:03,700
So he chooses not to ever break his fast.

848
00:57:04,160 --> 00:57:05,500
Every day he's fasting.

849
00:57:05,740 --> 00:57:06,720
As if it's Ramadan.

850
00:57:07,240 --> 00:57:08,140
It's gulu fitting.

851
00:57:09,720 --> 00:57:12,580
Or every day he's making kiamu led.

852
00:57:12,580 --> 00:57:16,630
From Isha after Isha to Fajr.

853
00:57:17,260 --> 00:57:18,000
Every day.

854
00:57:19,320 --> 00:57:22,600
Let's not forget that the Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam.

855
00:57:22,940 --> 00:57:25,600
One of the companions was reported to him.

856
00:57:26,720 --> 00:57:31,060
The wife reported to the brother who came to visit him.

857
00:57:31,460 --> 00:57:32,900
In Medina.

858
00:57:33,360 --> 00:57:36,460
And that one went to report to the Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam.

859
00:57:36,580 --> 00:57:40,620
This companion, that was Abdullah Ibn Amr al-As.

860
00:57:40,620 --> 00:57:43,800
He did notice to sleep in the night.

861
00:57:44,820 --> 00:57:47,260
And he would fast every day.

862
00:57:49,000 --> 00:57:50,240
So his wife was feeling.

863
00:57:50,560 --> 00:57:52,040
He would not come near the wife.

864
00:57:52,840 --> 00:57:55,260
The Prophet didn't like it Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam.

865
00:57:55,680 --> 00:58:00,720
Something similar to that was reported about Abul Zerrin al-Ghifari also.

866
00:58:02,180 --> 00:58:03,040
So Ekhwa.

867
00:58:03,740 --> 00:58:05,800
Those who go beyond limits.

868
00:58:07,340 --> 00:58:08,080
Ghalin Fidin.

869
00:58:08,120 --> 00:58:09,680
We just explained Gulu Fidin.

870
00:58:09,680 --> 00:58:12,720
For example fasting throughout the day time.

871
00:58:12,760 --> 00:58:13,920
Never breaking fast.

872
00:58:14,760 --> 00:58:16,680
Or never observing sleep.

873
00:58:16,780 --> 00:58:17,700
Not sleeping.

874
00:58:20,020 --> 00:58:24,020
Wa inna li jasadika alayka haqqan.

875
00:58:24,180 --> 00:58:26,200
And your body has a right over you.

876
00:58:26,480 --> 00:58:27,820
So sleep sometimes.

877
00:58:28,520 --> 00:58:29,640
Wake up sometimes.

878
00:58:30,880 --> 00:58:32,820
Some people abandon their wives.

879
00:58:33,160 --> 00:58:35,780
Some women abandon their husbands.

880
00:58:36,620 --> 00:58:37,920
And making kiamu led.

881
00:58:37,920 --> 00:58:39,140
And fasting.

882
00:58:40,040 --> 00:58:42,220
So that's why the husband cannot come near her.

883
00:58:42,940 --> 00:58:44,740
That's why she can't cook for her husband.

884
00:58:45,520 --> 00:58:46,060
This Gulu.

885
00:58:47,460 --> 00:58:49,960
So the Prophet said alayhi salatu wassalam.

886
00:58:50,260 --> 00:58:54,200
So in Fadim, in Ummati ila tana luhu ma shafa'ati.

887
00:58:54,540 --> 00:58:56,340
Two groups of people in my ummah.

888
00:58:56,620 --> 00:58:58,900
My special Shafa'a.

889
00:58:59,580 --> 00:59:03,540
Mentioned for special people in special situations will not reach them.

890
00:59:04,500 --> 00:59:05,700
The first one.

891
00:59:07,220 --> 00:59:09,560
Sultanun zhaloumun ghashoum.

892
00:59:09,880 --> 00:59:10,700
The Sultan.

893
00:59:11,180 --> 00:59:11,980
The President.

894
00:59:12,160 --> 00:59:12,780
The Governor.

895
00:59:13,040 --> 00:59:13,560
The head.

896
00:59:13,740 --> 00:59:15,560
The one with constituted authority.

897
00:59:16,060 --> 00:59:18,000
But he is zhaloum.

898
00:59:18,120 --> 00:59:20,020
Very wickedly unjust.

899
00:59:21,440 --> 00:59:21,760
Ghashoum.

900
00:59:22,420 --> 00:59:23,260
He is wicked.

901
00:59:24,900 --> 00:59:25,540
Jabbar.

902
00:59:26,540 --> 00:59:27,180
Wicked.

903
00:59:28,720 --> 00:59:30,880
The Shafa'a of the Prophet will not reach him.

904
00:59:30,920 --> 00:59:31,920
Alayhi salatu wassalam.

905
00:59:31,920 --> 00:59:35,260
Wa ghalim fi deen.

906
00:59:37,220 --> 00:59:42,320
And those who go beyond limits in the maqas of their religion.

907
00:59:42,960 --> 00:59:45,700
Yushhidu alayhim.

908
00:59:46,960 --> 00:59:50,060
Yushhadu alayhim wa yutabarra'u minhum.

909
00:59:51,520 --> 00:59:53,200
These people.

910
00:59:54,040 --> 00:59:57,060
Aw yushhadu alayhim wa yutabarra'u minhum.

911
00:59:57,860 --> 01:00:01,340
The Prophet salallahu alayhi wa alayhi wassalam.

912
01:00:01,820 --> 01:00:02,840
He will see them.

913
01:00:03,580 --> 01:00:06,140
And he will disconnect himself from them.

914
01:00:07,000 --> 01:00:09,140
Salallahu alayhi wa alayhi wassalam.

915
01:00:09,620 --> 01:00:13,140
The ruler who is unjust and wicked to the people.

916
01:00:14,340 --> 01:00:19,460
And those who go beyond limits in the maqas of their deen.

917
01:00:20,140 --> 01:00:21,800
May Allah protect all of us.

918
01:00:21,800 --> 01:00:26,660
This hadith occurs in the maujam of al-Imam al-Tabrani.

919
01:00:26,880 --> 01:00:29,240
We said that this is not as weak.

920
01:00:29,980 --> 01:00:31,440
But the hadith is tzahir.

921
01:00:32,240 --> 01:00:34,820
So al-Imam al-Bahabi said, aghlabu dha'if.

922
01:00:35,060 --> 01:00:37,040
Yani al-aghlab ibn Tamim.

923
01:00:37,760 --> 01:00:39,620
He's a weak reporter of hadith.

924
01:00:40,020 --> 01:00:41,820
Wa qod'u wa'u ibn al-Mubarak.

925
01:00:42,480 --> 01:00:46,240
But this report has also been collected by al-Imam ibn al-Mubarak.

926
01:00:47,120 --> 01:00:48,240
He said...

927
01:01:08,920 --> 01:01:12,380
Using a similar thing of report.

928
01:01:13,420 --> 01:01:14,560
Al-Imam al-Bahabi said...

929
01:01:18,900 --> 01:01:23,320
It was mentioned that we don't know who he was.

930
01:01:23,780 --> 01:01:25,240
Al-Imam al-Bahabi said...

931
01:01:27,200 --> 01:01:29,240
But there are other bigger reports.

932
01:01:29,980 --> 01:01:31,820
Like that of al-Imam ibn al-Adeel.

933
01:01:31,920 --> 01:01:33,240
Who mentioned that...

934
01:01:39,060 --> 01:01:41,740
So muna'i, his reports are Hasan.

935
01:01:42,560 --> 01:01:44,300
But that's why al-Imam al-Bahabi said...

936
01:01:45,240 --> 01:01:47,820
It is not known who he was.

937
01:01:48,340 --> 01:01:51,700
Ibn al-Adeel has spoken earlier that we know him.

938
01:01:53,340 --> 01:01:56,220
Al-Adeel shows that no matter how well-grounded you are,

939
01:01:56,460 --> 01:01:57,480
some things will miss you.

940
01:01:57,620 --> 01:01:58,520
You say you don't know.

941
01:01:58,520 --> 01:01:59,900
Others say we know it.

942
01:02:00,740 --> 01:02:02,500
People had known it before you.

943
01:02:03,220 --> 01:02:07,100
But the point of reference here is that...

944
01:02:10,520 --> 01:02:16,360
The head, the imam, the leader, the president, the governor,

945
01:02:16,720 --> 01:02:18,960
who is unjust and wicked,

946
01:02:20,100 --> 01:02:22,380
they will not gain the Shafa'ah of the Prophet,

947
01:02:22,480 --> 01:02:25,400
sallallahu alayhi wa sallam, the day of Ki'aam.

948
01:02:25,980 --> 01:02:28,380
May Allah protect all of us from this evil.

949
01:02:29,500 --> 01:02:32,860
The evil of being a wicked leader and head.

950
01:02:34,120 --> 01:02:35,180
Wicked principal.

951
01:02:37,480 --> 01:02:38,520
Wicked HM.

952
01:02:39,140 --> 01:02:41,120
And facts, wicked husband.

953
01:02:42,580 --> 01:02:44,940
All of these come under this category.

954
01:02:46,560 --> 01:02:49,040
Allah, we beg your protection, protect us.

955
01:02:49,600 --> 01:02:51,780
Ya'zal jalal walaykoum.

956
01:02:52,540 --> 01:02:55,440
I think we can look at the questions,

957
01:02:55,480 --> 01:02:57,060
if we have one or two questions,

958
01:02:57,100 --> 01:02:59,120
before we call it the day about the Rahman.

959
01:03:00,700 --> 01:03:02,080
Do we have a question?

960
01:03:02,840 --> 01:03:05,420
Or we just call it the day about the Rahman?

961
01:03:06,260 --> 01:03:10,180
I just saw now that the time has been fast spent.

962
01:03:13,820 --> 01:03:14,860
About the Rahman.

963
01:03:23,540 --> 01:03:25,440
About the Rahman, are you there?

964
01:03:30,160 --> 01:03:32,540
Okay, we can call it the day today.

965
01:03:34,840 --> 01:03:35,360
Ameen.

966
01:03:39,180 --> 01:03:41,260
Should we call it the day today?

967
01:03:41,700 --> 01:03:42,080
Okay.

968
01:03:43,700 --> 01:03:46,200
We come back to class on this issue.

969
01:03:48,120 --> 01:03:51,440
Assalamu alaikum wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu.

970
01:03:51,580 --> 01:03:53,860
Wa alaikum wa salamu alaikum wa barakatuhu.

971
01:03:53,860 --> 01:03:55,840
Assalamu alaikum wa barakatuhu.

972
01:03:55,840 --> 01:03:56,020
Ameen.

